From 241767804bfae439b0c100f1eaa90b94c5199100 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand-build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:26:55 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Spatiand: built for Android libc: frames to the room in
 Android hardware buffers

Each window's frame is copied on the GPU into an Android hardware buffer, sent once to Spatiand's
room through a socket that stands as a dmabuf's file, marked with Spatiand's own modifier, which
the room's EGL turns back into the buffer (android/eglshim in Spatiand): no copy in memory on
either side. ANGLE takes such buffers as EGLImages on Android's libc
(third_party/angle linux/AHardwareBufferImageSiblingVkSpatiand, as its Android build does), with
Vulkan's import from Android's buffers on. The buffer allocator's mapper is loaded before the
GPU sandbox. A frame goes to the room once its fence says the GPU has drawn it, looked at every
millisecond without holding the thread. Frames in flight keep their places through a resize, where
the queue was read past its end. Where the room offers no such modifier, frames are read back as
before.
---
 content/gpu/gpu_main.cc                       |  28 ++
 .../gpu/gl_surface_egl_readback_wayland.cc    | 296 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../gpu/gl_surface_egl_readback_wayland.h     |  48 +++
 3 files changed, 372 insertions(+)

